        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d433dafe-364a-56ef-a742-3d18763b204c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bo Diddley, Paul Samwell-Smith, Eric Clapton, Jeff Beck, Jimmy Page\n- Bands: The Yardbirds, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Who, The Clash, Parliament-Funkadelic\n- Songs: \"Before You Accuse Me\"\n- Places: London, Richmond, Surrey\n- Topics: rock and roll, blues, R&B\n\nFacts:\n- Bo Diddley, born Ellas Otha Bates and later known as Ellas McDaniel, was born on December 30, 1928.\n- Bo Diddley was an American R&B singer, guitarist, songwriter, and music producer who played a key role in the transition from the blues to rock and roll.\n- The song \"Before You Accuse Me\" was written and recorded by Bo Diddley in 1957.\n- Paul Samwell-Smith was born Paul Smith on May 8, 1943, in Richmond, Surrey.\n- The Yardbirds formed in London in 1963 as an English rock band.\n- Paul Samwell-Smith was a founding member and bassist of The Yardbirds.\n- The Yardbirds became a group associated with notable musicians including Jeff Beck, Eric Clapton, and Jimmy Page.\n- Bo Diddley influenced artists including Elvis Presley, Buddy Holly, the Beatles, the Rolling Stones, the Yardbirds, Eric Clapton, the Who, Jimi Hendrix, George Thorogood, Parliament-Funkadelic, and The Clash.\n- Bo Diddley died on June 2, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
